+## 2. Inputs and method
+
+| Source | What it gave |
+|---|---|
+| README.md, ROADMAP §8 | The promise and the simplicity budget; every suggestion below fits it (wording, existing selects, the drawer, "Location → within N km") |
+| lead.md from "Fix wave 5, data lane" on, and fix waves 3–4 | What changed since wave 1 |
+| persona-beta-25-34.md (wave 1) | B1–B5 and I1–I18 to re-check (§6) |
+| `<dist>/beta/api/jobs/*.json` unpacked with `unpackJobs` from `<dist>/beta/api.js`; `<dist>/beta/api/desc/<slug>/<id>.json` | Choosing goals the data can serve; checking every odd number against the posted text |
+| `public/app.js`, `public/features/shared.js`, `public/features/roles.js` (as built in `<dist>/beta/`) | Read only after something looked wrong on screen, to name the owner |
+
+- **Driving.** One long-lived Chromium (`/opt/pw-browsers/chromium-1194`) behind a small local driver
+  (`<scratch>/persona-beta-2-25-34/driver.mjs`, 127.0.0.1 only) with one context per person and device;
+  each step is a snippet in `<scratch>/persona-beta-2-25-34/s/`. Phones use isMobile, hasTouch, the
+  phone-sizes user agents, taps and CDP touch swipes for the results sheet; laptops use clicks and typing.
+- **Times.** "App" is measured on this shared 4-CPU machine with no throttling, from the tap to the result,
+  minus the fixed settle waits in my scripts; the 1-minute load average is given (3.3–15.5 during the run,
+  with four other reviewers). "Person" is my estimate of reading and deciding.
+- **Coming back later.** A new context from the saved storage state, no link; `s/later.mjs` back-dates
+  `melon.saved[].lastSeenAt` and the `melon.seen.*` stamps by 2–10 days and drops 1–2 ids from `seen`, so
+  "N new" can be tested on a frozen crawl.
+- **Not reported** (per the lead's wave-1 rule): the badge's "About every 6 hours" on a week-old local
+  snapshot, and the grey "Basemap unavailable" map.
+- **Severity.** Broken = a number or label that is wrong or misleading, or a blocked task; each was checked
+  against the posting text or the code. Everything else is Improve, ranked by how many of the five it helps.
